WEBVTT

00:00.990 --> 00:06.930
Zankoku na tenshi no you ni

00:00.990 --> 00:06.930
Just like the cruel angel

00:06.930 --> 00:14.590
Shounen yo shinwa ni nare

00:06.930 --> 00:14.590
Young boy, become a legend

00:18.990 --> 00:22.410
2D4U PRESENTS:

00:22.770 --> 00:25.810
Aoi kaze ga ima

00:22.770 --> 00:25.810
Even though the untested breeze...

00:25.810 --> 00:29.510
mune no doa o tataitemo

00:25.810 --> 00:29.510
...taps at the door to your heart

00:29.510 --> 00:36.970
Watashi dake o tada mitsumete hohoenderu anata

00:29.510 --> 00:36.970
You just look solely at me and smile

00:37.560 --> 00:44.500
Sotto fureru mono motomeru koto ni muchuu de

00:37.560 --> 00:44.500
So intent on seeking out that gentle touch

00:44.500 --> 00:51.400
Unmei sae mada shiranai itaike na hitomi

00:44.500 --> 00:51.400
Such innocent eyes, still ignorant of their destiny

00:52.000 --> 00:55.750
Dakedo itsuka kizuku deshou

00:52.000 --> 00:55.750
But someday, you are sure to realize...

00:55.750 --> 00:58.340
sono senaka ni wa

00:55.750 --> 00:58.340
...that upon your back

00:59.510 --> 01:02.960
Haruka mirai mezasu tame

00:59.510 --> 01:02.960
You have the wings with which to fly...

01:02.960 --> 01:06.310
no hane ga aru koto

01:02.960 --> 01:06.310
...towards the distant future

01:06.990 --> 01:10.690
Zankoku na tenshi no teeze

01:06.990 --> 01:10.690
The cruel angel's thesis

01:10.690 --> 01:14.430
Madobe kara yagate tobidatsu

01:10.690 --> 01:14.430
Soon, you will take flight from the windowsill

01:14.430 --> 01:18.200
Hotobashiru atsui patosu de

01:14.430 --> 01:18.200
With your torrent of ardent pathos

01:18.200 --> 01:21.900
Omoide o uragiru nara

01:18.200 --> 01:21.900
If you are to betray our memories

01:21.900 --> 01:25.540
Kono sora o daite kagayaku

01:21.900 --> 01:25.540
You, who embrace these heavens and shine

01:25.540 --> 01:29.270
Shounen yo shinwa ni nare

01:25.540 --> 01:29.270
Young boy, become a legend

01:38.780 --> 01:41.200
Cool! I won, I won!

01:44.120 --> 01:47.620
Coin Cleaning
24 Hours OK

01:47.620 --> 01:48.420
Done
Take Out

01:48.540 --> 01:50.540
Thank you very much

01:49.130 --> 01:52.670
Boy, the cost of doing laundry
has been killing me lately.

01:52.670 --> 01:56.470
I wish I at least had the time
to wash my own clothes.

01:56.470 --> 01:59.720
You should appreciate the fact you can
at least sleep at home.

01:59.720 --> 02:01.850
Please make
sure to take
your pass.

01:59.720 --> 02:01.850
Take Out

02:01.970 --> 02:02.930
TRAIN APPROACHING

02:08.730 --> 02:10.520
Hello, Vice Commander.

02:11.610 --> 02:13.570
Good morning, Sir.

02:14.230 --> 02:15.690
Good morning, Sir!

02:15.690 --> 02:17.200
Morning.

02:19.530 --> 02:21.700
You're quite early today.

02:21.700 --> 02:24.540
Well, I have to go up top in Ikari's place.

02:24.540 --> 02:27.460
I see. Isn't today the City Council's
regular meeting?

02:27.460 --> 02:29.540
It's a pointless job.

02:29.540 --> 02:33.500
Ikari has always thrust the sundry tasks onto me.

02:33.500 --> 02:36.090
Without the Magi, I'd be lost.

02:36.090 --> 02:39.550
Speaking of which, the city elections
are approaching up there, right?

02:39.550 --> 02:41.760
The City Council is merely a shell.

02:41.760 --> 02:45.180
The municipal government, after all,
is in fact run by the Magi.

02:45.180 --> 02:48.520
The Magi? You mean the
three supercomputers?

02:48.520 --> 02:51.770
Government by majority decision
of three different computers.

02:51.770 --> 02:55.150
It's a system that is properly in line
with the fundamentals of democracy.

02:55.150 --> 02:58.240
And the council just obeys their decisions?

02:58.240 --> 03:01.450
It's a most efficient form of government.

03:01.450 --> 03:03.320
That's a city of science for you.

03:03.320 --> 03:05.870
It's really an era where science reigns supreme.

03:05.870 --> 03:07.700
Talk about an old-fashioned line.

03:07.700 --> 03:11.330
Come to think of it, you're running
an experiment on Unit 00, aren't you?

03:11.330 --> 03:16.550
Yes, we're going to run the second
prolonged activation test at 10:30.

03:16.550 --> 03:18.380
I'm looking forward to good news.

03:21.510 --> 03:23.470
Abort experiment! Cut the circuits!

03:26.310 --> 03:28.020
Switching circuits.

03:28.020 --> 03:29.730
Power supply being restored.

03:32.560 --> 03:34.520
This is still the problem here, huh?

03:34.520 --> 03:36.770
Yes, the fact that the conversion efficiency

03:36.770 --> 03:39.610
is 0.008 lower than our
theoretical value concerns me.

03:39.610 --> 03:42.280
It's just barely within tolerance, though,

03:42.280 --> 03:43.780
but what do we do?

03:43.780 --> 03:45.320
Let's try it again using the same configuration,

03:45.320 --> 03:48.080
but lower the reciprocal
conversion rate by 0.01.

03:48.080 --> 03:49.040
Roger.

03:49.040 --> 03:51.410
Now, let's recommence the
reactivation experiment.

03:51.460 --> 03:55.170
EPISODE 11
IN THE STILL DARKNESS

03:57.250 --> 03:59.630
Hey, hold up!

04:07.310 --> 04:09.810
Man, that was a run!

04:10.930 --> 04:13.270
You've certainly got a black expression.

04:13.270 --> 04:16.230
It's from seeing your loathsome face
first thing in the morning.

04:16.560 --> 04:18.900
Yes, please hold for just a moment.

04:30.580 --> 04:32.370
What?

04:32.910 --> 04:34.670
Um, Father...

04:34.670 --> 04:36.460
What is it? Spit it out!

04:40.250 --> 04:42.510
Well...

04:42.510 --> 04:44.840
Actually today...

04:44.840 --> 04:49.010
We were told to tell our parents...

04:50.060 --> 04:55.560
...that they're having a career discussion
interview at school.

04:55.560 --> 04:59.320
I've delegated all such things
to Captain Katsuragi.

04:59.320 --> 05:01.530
Don't call me over such nonsense.

05:02.280 --> 05:04.150
Don't forward any more of these calls to...

05:08.120 --> 05:09.160
Oh?

05:09.160 --> 05:10.240
A blackout?

05:10.240 --> 05:12.910
No way. That's not possible.

05:13.870 --> 05:16.540
That's strange. Do you suppose
there was an accident?

05:16.540 --> 05:18.750
Maybe Akagi messed up an experiment?

05:20.090 --> 05:21.800
The main power supply has been interrupted.

05:22.460 --> 05:24.260
Voltage level is zero!

05:26.590 --> 05:28.510
It wasn't me.

05:28.510 --> 05:30.180
What do you think?

05:30.180 --> 05:32.850
Well, it'll switch to the backup
power supply soon.

05:33.220 --> 05:35.890
It's no good, the backup circuits
aren't connecting.

05:35.890 --> 05:37.400
That can't be!

05:37.400 --> 05:39.230
Which circuits are still functioning?

05:39.230 --> 05:44.740
A total of one point two percent!
Only the old circuits from number 2567!

05:44.740 --> 05:48.820
Route all remaining power supplies
to maintaining the Magi and Central Dogma.

05:48.820 --> 05:51.580
But that will interfere with life support systems.

05:51.580 --> 05:53.330
I don't care! That's our top priority!

05:53.330 --> 05:54.750
Press
Button
To
Cross

05:53.540 --> 05:58.620
<i><i>Aiming for a politics that everyone can love,
with justice and truth...</i></i>

05:56.500 --> 05:59.670
Boy, she's such a lazy slob.

05:59.670 --> 06:04.670
Can't Captain Katsuragi at least
pick up her own laundry?

06:05.010 --> 06:06.590
Press
Button
To
Cross

06:06.760 --> 06:07.800
What?

06:08.680 --> 06:12.560
Maybe Commander Ikari
was just really busy?

06:12.560 --> 06:13.930
I don't know...

06:13.930 --> 06:17.890
It wasn't like he hung up, but more like
a mechanical failure.

06:17.890 --> 06:19.690
You know, you ARE a man.

06:19.690 --> 06:22.770
Why don't you stop worrying
about every little detail?

06:27.900 --> 06:28.650
What?

06:31.410 --> 06:34.540
What are you doing? Here, let me try that!

06:41.380 --> 06:44.250
Damn! It must be broken!

06:51.180 --> 06:53.260
Anyway, let's hurry to the command center.

06:53.260 --> 06:55.310
It's already been down for seven minutes!

06:55.310 --> 06:57.140
This isn't normal.

06:57.140 --> 06:58.270
What's the power system here?

06:58.270 --> 07:00.980
There are three systems, main, sub, and reserve.

07:00.980 --> 07:03.860
It's unthinkable that all three
would fail simultaneously.

07:04.520 --> 07:06.570
Which means...

07:06.570 --> 07:08.950
We should assume that the breakers
didn't fail on their own,

07:08.950 --> 07:11.610
but were taken down on purpose.

07:11.610 --> 07:12.820
Regardless of the cause,

07:12.820 --> 07:15.790
it would be disastrous if an Angel
were to attack right now.

07:15.990 --> 07:18.960
Radar has detected an unidentified object.

07:18.960 --> 07:21.580
Projected landing point is in
the former Atami region.

07:21.620 --> 07:24.920
PROJECTED COURSE

07:21.620 --> 07:24.920
PREPARED BY
CENTRAL ALERT CONTROL
COMMAND CENTER

07:22.460 --> 07:24.920
It's likely the eighth one.

07:24.920 --> 07:26.840
I agree, it must be an Angel.

07:24.960 --> 07:27.630
Fuchu General Supreme Command Center

07:26.840 --> 07:28.010
What are we going to do?

07:27.670 --> 07:30.380
Integrated Alert Control Room

07:28.010 --> 07:31.300
Go to alert status for now.
That's the procedure, after all.

07:32.300 --> 07:35.760
This one's destination is going to be
New Tokyo-3 anyway.

07:35.760 --> 07:40.060
I agree. Well, there's nothing we need to do.

07:36.560 --> 07:40.060
Projected Course

07:43.980 --> 07:47.400
22ND ALERT GROUP
OLD OMAEZAKI S.S.

07:44.480 --> 07:46.190
The Angel has landed.

07:46.190 --> 07:47.730
It's still advancing.

07:47.730 --> 07:49.740
What about New Tokyo-3?

07:49.740 --> 07:51.740
Still no response.

07:51.740 --> 07:54.370
What in the hell are those Nerv guys doing?

07:54.740 --> 07:58.200
I thought gangway ladders were decorative
holdovers from the past.

07:58.200 --> 08:00.710
Who'd have thought I'd be using one?

08:00.710 --> 08:02.790
To prepare is to prevent.

08:06.790 --> 08:08.590
This one doesn't work either!

08:08.590 --> 08:11.260
None of the facilities work. This is odd.

08:11.260 --> 08:13.260
Does that mean that something
happened down below?

08:13.260 --> 08:15.300
It would be natural to assume that.

08:15.890 --> 08:19.720
In any case, let's try to make contact
with Nerv Headquarters.

08:19.720 --> 08:21.890
No good, the emergency phones aren't
getting through either.

08:22.770 --> 08:26.190
No good, Line 77 won't connect either.

08:26.190 --> 08:28.110
No, no response.

08:29.070 --> 08:32.860
Not here either. The emergency
landline is down too.

08:32.860 --> 08:33.700
What do we do now?

08:42.200 --> 08:43.460
What're you doing?

08:43.460 --> 08:46.790
What are you, stupid?
It's the emergency manual!

08:46.790 --> 08:48.840
Anyway, let's go to headquarters.

08:48.840 --> 08:53.170
Yeah, but first let's decide on a group leader
before we take action.

08:54.430 --> 08:57.220
And naturally, I am the leader.

08:57.220 --> 08:58.390
No objections, I assume?

09:00.100 --> 09:02.100
Now, let's go.

09:02.100 --> 09:04.730
We can get below through Route 07 over here.

09:05.730 --> 09:07.980
But the doors won't work, will they?

09:09.400 --> 09:11.360
Manual door...

09:11.360 --> 09:13.860
Okay, Shinji, you're up.

09:15.820 --> 09:20.790
Sheesh! You only rely on people
at times like this!

09:22.330 --> 09:26.120
Damn those Joint Staff bastards!
They only rely on us at times like this.

09:26.120 --> 09:28.580
What does the government say?

09:28.580 --> 09:31.630
Those bastards in Tokyo-2?
They're apparently getting ready to run.

09:31.630 --> 09:33.050
Beware of Forest Fires

09:34.220 --> 09:36.510
The Angel is still active and advancing.

09:36.930 --> 09:40.220
In any case, get in contact with
the people at Nerv.

09:40.220 --> 09:42.140
But how?

09:42.140 --> 09:43.390
By actually going there.

09:45.770 --> 09:48.310
This is the 3rd District ASDF!

09:48.310 --> 09:51.900
An unidentified object is moving
toward this area.

09:51.900 --> 09:54.320
All residents must evacuate
to their designated shelters.

09:54.320 --> 09:57.610
Big trouble! I've got to report this
to Headquarters right away!

09:59.370 --> 10:01.330
But how?

10:03.040 --> 10:06.290
<i><i>Remember Takahashi remains calm
even in situations like this!</i></i>

10:06.290 --> 10:09.130
<i><i>Please support candidate Takahashi!</i></i>

10:09.830 --> 10:11.090
Lucky!

10:11.090 --> 10:14.050
But you know, it sure is hot.

10:14.050 --> 10:16.380
Yeah, the air conditioners are out too.

10:16.380 --> 10:20.180
Katsuragi, if you're so hot,
why don't you take off your shirt?

10:20.510 --> 10:22.850
There's no reason for shyness
between you and me.

10:24.140 --> 10:27.850
Don't get any funny ideas just because
we're in this situation.

10:27.850 --> 10:28.850
Okay, okay!

10:28.850 --> 10:32.730
This is bad. Now the air is getting stagnant.

10:32.730 --> 10:35.940
To think this facility represents the most
advanced technology on Earth...

10:35.940 --> 10:38.570
But look at the Commander
and Vice Commander.

10:38.570 --> 10:40.950
Even this heat isn't getting to them at all.

10:43.490 --> 10:46.000
For Fire Prevention

10:47.080 --> 10:49.000
It's lukewarm.

10:49.000 --> 10:49.920
Yeah.

11:00.220 --> 11:04.470
Pursuant to the declaration of a state
of emergency in this district,

11:02.600 --> 11:04.810
Nozomu Takahashi

11:04.470 --> 11:06.600
emergency vehicle, passing through!

11:06.600 --> 11:08.430
Excuse me, that's a dead end!

11:08.430 --> 11:10.140
It's okay! Charge!

11:10.140 --> 11:11.900
This is an emergency, after all!

11:11.900 --> 11:12.900
Roger!

11:12.900 --> 11:15.320
No! Stop the car!

11:16.150 --> 11:19.200
This Geo-Front was designed to be
a self-sufficient colony,

11:19.200 --> 11:22.700
even when isolated from the outside.

11:22.700 --> 11:27.620
Theoretically, it's impossible for all of
the power sources to fail at once.

11:27.620 --> 11:30.040
Which means that someone
did it deliberately, correct?

11:30.040 --> 11:32.710
Their purpose is likely to be
to investigate this facility.

11:32.710 --> 11:35.920
So they could determine HQ's structure
through the progress of restoration?

11:35.920 --> 11:38.090
Disrespectful bastards.

11:38.090 --> 11:40.590
I'll run a dummy program through the Magi.

11:40.590 --> 11:43.640
That will make it harder for them
to get a complete picture.

11:43.640 --> 11:45.010
I'll leave it to you.

11:44.470 --> 11:45.800
Yes, Sir.

11:45.800 --> 11:48.270
The first havoc wreaked upon our headquarters
wasn't caused by an Angel,

11:48.270 --> 11:51.890
but by another member of our species.
Just goes to show.

11:51.890 --> 11:54.940
Ultimately, the enemy of mankind is mankind.

11:55.480 --> 11:58.150
This would normally take only two minutes.

11:58.150 --> 12:00.360
Is this really a corridor?

12:00.360 --> 12:03.700
Once we get over there, we should be able to
come out in the Geo-Front.

12:04.780 --> 12:07.450
I've heard that from you four times already.

12:07.450 --> 12:09.790
You really are a nitpicky man!

12:09.790 --> 12:12.000
You're always focusing on the stupidest things.

12:12.000 --> 12:13.000
Quiet.

12:13.000 --> 12:14.790
What now, Miss Perfect?

12:14.790 --> 12:16.170
Someone's voice.

12:20.300 --> 12:21.760
Ang... proaching...

12:22.260 --> 12:23.880
That's Mr. Hyuga!

12:23.880 --> 12:27.350
Hey! Hey! Hey!

12:27.350 --> 12:31.640
An Angel is approaching!
Repeat, an Angel is approaching!

12:32.180 --> 12:33.850
An Angel is approaching?!

12:33.850 --> 12:36.480
There's no time to waste. Let's take a short cut.

12:36.480 --> 12:39.440
I'm the leader! Don't just take over!

12:39.440 --> 12:41.030
So where's this short cut?

12:42.530 --> 12:46.410
This may be the quickest way,
but we look really lame.

12:46.990 --> 12:50.160
Say, what do you suppose the Angels are?

12:50.160 --> 12:52.330
Why are you talking about that
at a time like this?

12:52.330 --> 12:57.330
Angels, messengers of God, enemies named
after servants of Heaven.

12:57.880 --> 12:59.380
Why are we fighting them?

12:59.380 --> 13:00.750
What are you, stupid?

13:00.750 --> 13:03.220
Strange beings are attacking us.

13:03.220 --> 13:06.260
If you're going through a fire, you've got to
brush away the embers, of course!

13:09.510 --> 13:10.680
To the right!

13:10.680 --> 13:12.470
I think it's left.

13:12.470 --> 13:14.180
Oh, be quiet!

13:14.180 --> 13:15.810
What do you think, Shinji?

13:15.810 --> 13:17.020
Well...

13:18.900 --> 13:20.110
I wonder?

13:20.110 --> 13:23.940
Honestly! I'm the leader,
so just shut up and follow me!

13:26.570 --> 13:29.830
I still think this is weird. We're going uphill.

13:29.830 --> 13:33.250
What do you mean, you still think?
You're such a nag!

13:36.290 --> 13:38.670
Look, this has got to be it this time!

13:56.560 --> 13:58.810
Well, we've visually confirmed
the Angel's presence.

13:58.810 --> 14:01.070
Now, we know we have to hurry.

14:04.030 --> 14:08.240
Angel is approaching! Immediate Eva
dispatch will be necessary!

14:08.240 --> 14:09.370
Oh, no!

14:09.370 --> 14:11.200
Fuyutsuki, I'll leave the rest to you.

14:11.200 --> 14:12.370
Ikari?

14:12.370 --> 14:15.660
I'll start preparing for the Eva launch in the cage.

14:15.660 --> 14:17.250
Don't tell me...

14:17.250 --> 14:19.040
Manually?

14:19.040 --> 14:20.960
There's an emergency diesel generator.

14:20.960 --> 14:22.590
But...

14:23.960 --> 14:25.630
We have no pilots.

14:27.260 --> 14:28.840
Not again!

14:30.970 --> 14:32.180
This way.

14:39.810 --> 14:42.560
I've heard that you're
Commander Ikari's favorite.

14:43.730 --> 14:47.240
I guess being Miss Perfect,
the teacher's pet, really shows.

14:47.240 --> 14:48.900
Let's not do this now.

14:48.900 --> 14:51.240
You always get to look all smug.

14:54.160 --> 14:57.700
Don't think that being favored means
that you can mess with me!

14:57.700 --> 14:59.210
I'm not messing with you.

15:00.870 --> 15:03.540
And I'm not favored either.

15:05.000 --> 15:06.550
I know that quite well.

15:06.550 --> 15:09.970
Heave ho! Heave ho!

15:14.850 --> 15:16.100
Roger.

15:16.100 --> 15:18.770
Ejection of the terminal plug is complete.

15:18.770 --> 15:21.850
Good, prepare to insert the entry plug
for all three units.

15:21.850 --> 15:23.940
But the pilots aren't here yet.

15:23.940 --> 15:26.230
Don't worry, they'll come without fail.

15:27.860 --> 15:30.900
I can't open this with my hands.

15:31.610 --> 15:35.830
It can't be helped. We'll have to break
into a duct to get through.

15:35.830 --> 15:38.080
This First Child is scary!

15:38.080 --> 15:40.830
She's the type who will do anything
to accomplish her objectives.

15:41.500 --> 15:43.580
In other words, a self-righteous bitch.

15:52.890 --> 15:55.050
The plug is fixed and ready.

15:55.050 --> 15:56.560
Now, we just have to wait for the kids.

16:00.560 --> 16:05.690
Don't you dare look forward!
If you do, I'll kill you!

16:06.360 --> 16:08.320
Stupid! Stupid! Stupid!

16:08.320 --> 16:10.110
Didn't I just say not to look?!

16:10.110 --> 16:12.860
I couldn't help it! I've got to...

16:16.910 --> 16:18.240
You guys!

16:20.450 --> 16:22.370
All units, prepare for entry!

16:22.370 --> 16:24.500
Roger, open the hatches manually.

16:24.790 --> 16:26.080
How are the Evas?

16:26.420 --> 16:28.210
They're in standby.

16:30.090 --> 16:32.170
But nothing's working.

16:32.170 --> 16:33.800
It was all done by hand.

16:34.430 --> 16:36.300
It was the Commander's idea.

16:36.300 --> 16:37.800
My father's?

16:40.600 --> 16:45.600
Commander Ikari had faith that you would come,
and prepared everything.

16:49.070 --> 16:51.530
Flywheel, ready for connection!

16:49.780 --> 16:52.320
All units, interior set.

16:51.530 --> 16:53.650
We're good! Run the cell motor!

16:59.950 --> 17:01.410
Plugs inserted.

17:01.410 --> 17:03.910
All units activated using backup power supply.

17:03.910 --> 17:06.000
Release the primary lock bolts.

17:09.460 --> 17:12.510
Hydraulic locks numbers 2
through 32, released.

17:12.800 --> 17:14.220
Zero pressure.

17:14.220 --> 17:15.800
The situation is free.

17:15.800 --> 17:19.850
Go ahead. Each unit, force open the restraints
under your own power.

17:19.850 --> 17:20.810
Head out!

17:40.660 --> 17:42.870
The target appears to have halted
directly above us!

17:43.950 --> 17:45.290
Get ready! Hurry up!

17:47.330 --> 17:49.710
The emergency batteries have been loaded!

17:49.710 --> 17:51.210
All right, we can do this!

17:51.210 --> 17:51.800
Launch!

17:59.550 --> 18:03.020
Geez! This is SO uncool!

18:03.020 --> 18:04.350
We're approaching the vertical shaft.

18:12.820 --> 18:16.190
This is still uncool.

18:21.700 --> 18:22.910
Watch out! Dodge!

18:27.750 --> 18:29.040
No!

19:04.490 --> 19:09.500
It appears the target is going to invade HQ
using a powerful liquid solvent.

19:09.500 --> 19:10.370
What'll we do?

19:10.370 --> 19:12.670
We're going to beat it, of course.

19:12.670 --> 19:14.340
Sure, but how?

19:14.340 --> 19:18.220
We dropped our rifles, and the battery
packs are running out.

19:18.220 --> 19:20.180
They won't last more than another three minutes.

19:20.880 --> 19:22.680
I have a plan.

19:22.680 --> 19:24.850
The one who stays here will be defense.

19:24.850 --> 19:26.520
Their job is to neutralize the AT Field,

19:26.520 --> 19:28.770
and to protect the offensive player
from the liquid solvent.

19:28.770 --> 19:33.310
The backup player will go down, pick up
the rifles, and hand them to the offense.

19:33.310 --> 19:36.900
The offense will then fire a volley
to destroy the target.

19:36.900 --> 19:38.320
Does that sound good?

19:38.320 --> 19:40.110
Fine. I will take the defense.

19:40.110 --> 19:41.660
Sorry, but it's not you.

19:41.860 --> 19:43.030
I'll do it.

19:43.030 --> 19:44.830
No way! It's dangerous!

19:45.620 --> 19:47.370
That's why.

19:47.370 --> 19:51.210
I don't want to stay indebted to you
from last time.

19:51.210 --> 19:54.040
Shinji's on offense. Miss Perfect is the backup.

19:54.040 --> 19:55.210
Got it?

19:55.500 --> 19:56.800
Understood.

20:00.090 --> 20:01.800
Okay, here we go!

20:03.260 --> 20:04.470
Gehen!

20:24.910 --> 20:25.660
Ayanami!

20:29.290 --> 20:30.580
Asuka, get out of the way!

20:43.510 --> 20:45.340
Now we're even.

20:46.800 --> 20:50.600
Oh, damn it! Why won't it open?!

20:50.600 --> 20:52.520
This is an emergency!

20:52.520 --> 20:55.560
I've gotta go!

20:56.270 --> 20:59.110
Hey, I told you not to look up!

20:59.110 --> 21:00.400
Yeah, yeah...

21:10.870 --> 21:11.870
Disgusting...

21:17.790 --> 21:21.670
It's ironic that the stars are so beautiful

21:21.670 --> 21:25.470
when there's no electricity or artificial lights.

21:25.470 --> 21:29.140
But without the lights, it doesn't feel
like anyone lives there.

21:32.890 --> 21:35.770
See? I feel much more comfortable this way.

21:35.770 --> 21:40.650
Man has always feared the darkness,
carving away at it with fire.

21:41.530 --> 21:43.400
How philosophical!

21:44.030 --> 21:47.530
Is that what makes mankind a special species?

21:48.070 --> 21:50.490
Is that why the Angels keep attacking us?

21:50.490 --> 21:52.200
What are you, stupid?

21:52.200 --> 21:54.790
There's no way to know that.

21:57.290 --> 22:00.750
TO BE CONTINUED

23:06.230 --> 23:06.990
PREVIEW

23:07.570 --> 23:10.530
Misato sublimates her frustration
into destroying the Angels.

23:10.530 --> 23:11.700
A past is revealed.

23:11.700 --> 23:14.660
However, the largest Angel yet,
flying in from the stratosphere,

23:14.660 --> 23:16.750
causes people to abandon hope.

23:16.750 --> 23:18.870
Next episode: "The Value of a Miracle"

23:18.200 --> 23:21.250
THE VALUE OF A MIRACLE

23:18.870 --> 23:20.580
Watch it with all your friends!
